# Archive = removed elsewhere

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`).

## Meaning

When a **page** or **section** is archived, it must leave **every live surface** — not merely be listed on an archive index while still showing in nav, collages, pickers, or other days.

## Pages

- Archiving a page (`archiveNavPage` / `btm_archived_pages_v1`) removes it from the live nav layout and keeps it out of `resolvedLinks`.
- Rebuild the nav after archive.
- Do not leave the page as a live main/WIP link “elsewhere.”

## Sections

- Archiving a vision section (`archiveTile` / `btm_archived_sections_v1`) removes it from the **current day and future days only** (`scrubArchivedSectionsEverywhere`). **Past days are not affected** — leave history alone.
- `addTile` must refuse globally archived focuses/titles.
- `+` section pickers (`sectionPresets` / `collectSectionPresets` / sec-picker) must **omit** archived sections so they cannot be re-added from presets.
- Archive index pages (`archived-sections.html`, `archived-pages.html`) are the only place they should remain reachable as archived.

## Never

- Archive on one day but leave the same section sitting on **current/future** days
- Scrub **past** days when archiving (never rewrite history)
- Keep an archived page in the hamburger main list
- Re-seed / auto-add an archived section back onto a collage
- Leave an archived section as a choice in the `+` section picker

## If something archived is still visible live

Scrub it immediately (nav rebuild + `scrubArchivedSectionsEverywhere`). Do not wait to be reminded.
